  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Thursday)\nIssued at 1232 PM MDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nUpper level ridge over the Rockies will shift east and expand \nover the central CONUS. This will result in very hot temperatures \nthis weekend into next week. Departing batch of monsoon moisture \nwill support scattered showers and storms into the evening as \ndiurnal heating allows for expansion in coverage this afternoon. \nLocally heavy rainfall will be possible given high PWATs and slow \nmovement. Upper ridge will begin to shift east Friday although a \nridge topping impulse will shift a trough across the southern \nCanada and the Dakotas, with the tail end of the trough stalling \nin the FA later tomorrow. Much warmer temps tomorrow with highs in\nthe 90s most places, with a few low 100s possible in areas on the\nPlains. Aforementioned upper trough may support a few isolated \nshowers or storms across NW SD in the afternoon, carried a low pop\nfor this. Separate weak impulse may also support a shower or \nstorm across northeast WY in the evening and so have also added \nlow pops there as well. Upper ridge will shift east Sat with very \nhot temps expected. Highs will reach 100 or higher for most \nlocations on the Plains, supporting adv level heat index readings.\nLow level moisture will deplete some with mixing, but sustained \nsoutherly flow will prevent the BL from drying out too much most \nplaces. This will help keep heat index readings higher, esp over \ncentral SD. Heat looks to persist at least through Tues, possibly \nlonger depending on how passing ridge periphery impulses affect \nthe ridge. Expect that there will be TS chances at times in this \nperiod as monsoon moisture advects around the NW side of the \nridge. This includes Sat when another monsoon wave will advect \naround the ridge in SW flow and into the FA later Sat, supporting \nhigh based TS chances. Gusty winds will be possible with any \nthunderstorms in this period given high based nature and near \ninverted-V profiles. Ridge will retrograde back west some by mid \nnext week, supporting slightly cooler but still hot temps, with \nexpected TS chances as the lee trough interacts will passing \nimpulses.",
